    #   - Block the column dimension j into tiles of size TILE_J.
    #   - For each (i, tile J), use small stack-allocated scratch arrays:
    #         Bij_tile[jj]       ≈ B[i, j] for j in this tile
    #         alpha_Bij_tile[jj] ≈ alpha * B[i, j]
    #         temp2_tile[jj]     ≈ temp2(i, j)
    #   - Interchange the original j- and k-loops inside each tile so that
    #     k becomes outer and the innermost loop runs over jj (columns in
    #     the tile). This yields unit-stride accesses in j for B and C,
    #     improving cache locality and enabling SIMD vectorization by the
    #     C compiler.
    #
    # The triangular dependency k < i is preserved, and each C[i, j] is still
    # scaled by beta exactly once, before any contributions from later rows.

    for i in seq(0, m):
        # Process columns in tiles of size TILE_J to improve cache locality.
        for J in seq(0, (n + TILE_J - 1) / TILE_J):

            # Tile-local scratch arrays:
            #   temp2_tile[jj]     accumulates temp2(i, j) for j in this tile.
            #   Bij_tile[jj]       caches B[i, j] so we read B's row i once.
            #   alpha_Bij_tile[jj] precomputes alpha * B[i, j] to avoid
            #                       redundant multiplications in the k-loop.
